/-!
## The rational lifting operators and their arithmetic bound

Results from §9 ("The rational lifting operators and their arithmetic bound") of
`blueprints/discrete-sw.tex`: the setup of §9, Blueprint Lemma 9.1 (`lem:liftkernel`) and
Blueprint Lemma 9.2 (`lem:arithmax`).

### Conventions

Mathlib Fourier sign and the lattice/torus conventions of section `Sampling`
(`latKernel m y = ∫_{[0,1)ⁿ} m(ξ) e(y · ξ) dξ`, `periodize`, `gridPt q b = b/q`). The fixed
parameters `(n, d, Ω, p)` enter through `M = paramM n d Ω p`, `ρ = paramRho n d Ω p`,
`r = paramR p` and `𝒰_N = paramGoodSet n d Ω p N` (Construction 8.2); `D = 2d`.

### Definitions (§9 setup)

* cutoffs: `liftCutoff n = χ` (`χ(ξ) = θ(2ξ)`, `θ = companionCutoff n`), and `χ̃ = θ` itself;
  the scaled cutoffs `liftChi … s = χ_s = χ(L_s ·)` and `liftChiT … s = χ̃_s = χ̃(L_s ·)`;
* scales (eq. (9.1), `eq:vs`): `liftN s = N_s = 2^s`, the constant `liftCStar = C_*`,
  `liftV … s = v_s = ⌈C_*(s+1)(1 + 2^{s/(2M)})⌉`, `liftL … s = L_s = 2^{v_s}`; the constant
  `liftCrho = C_{ρ,r}` is a choice from `goodBlocks_eps_threshold`;
* `liftRat s = 𝓡_s` (pairs `(a, q)` with `N_s/2 ≤ q < N_s`, `0 ≤ a < q`, `(a,q) = 1`);
* `gaussSum n d a q b = S(a/q, b/q) = q^{-n} ∑_{z mod q} e((a/q) P(z) - z · b/q)` (`eq:Gaussdef`,
  in the Mathlib sign: `∑_β S(α,β) e(β · y) = e(α P(y))`, `sum_gaussSum_mul_eC`);
* `liftSym … s a q m = Lift_{s,a/q}[m]` (`eq:Liftdef`), `liftA … s a q = A_{s,a/q}`,
  `liftD … s m = D_s[m] = ∑_{β ∈ 𝒰_{N_s}} (m χ̃_s)_per(· - β)`; `liftPhi … s = φ_s = 𝓕⁻ χ_s`.

### Results

* eq. (9.2) (`eq:scalerequirements`): `exists_liftCStar`, `liftV_ge`, `four_div_liftL_le`;
  consequences `liftEps_threshold` (hypothesis (7.1) with `ε = 4/L_s`), `lift_transference`
  (Theorem 7.7 for `𝒰_{N_s}` with `ε = 4/L_s`) and `liftBump_center_atMostOne` (disjointness of
  the enlarged bumps at the centers of `𝒰_{N_s}`); `liftChi_mul_liftChiT` (`χ_s χ̃_s = χ_s`);
* Blueprint Lemma 9.1 (`lem:liftkernel`): `latKernel_liftSym`, `latKernel_liftSym_of_bdd`,
  `latKernel_liftA`, and the envelope bound `norm_liftPhi_le` (`|φ_s(y)| ≤ C B_{L_s}(y)`).
* Blueprint Lemma 9.2 (`lem:arithmax`): eq. (9.5) `arith_maximal_decay`
  (`‖sup_{α ∈ 𝓡_s} |A_{s,α} f|‖₂ ≤ C 2^{-γ s} ‖f‖₂`) and eq. (9.6)
  `arith_maximal_decay_vector` (the `ℓ^t(ℓ²)` bound, `1 < t < ∞`, with `δ_t = γ min(2/t, 2/t')`).
* Blueprint Lemma 9.3 (`lem:liftsquare`): eq. (9.8) `liftSym_eq_liftA_mul_liftD` (symbols), with
  the operator forms `latMult_liftSym_eq_tsum` (`Lift[m](D) f = Ǎ * (D_s[m](D) f)`) and
  `latMult_liftSym_eq_latMult` (when `D_s[m](D) f ∈ ℓ¹`); eq. (9.9) `lift_square_two`; eq. (9.10)
  `lift_square_p`. Since `D_s[m](D) f` need not be in `ℓ¹` for merely bounded `m`, eq. (9.6) is
  first extended to bounded inputs (`arith_maximal_decay_vector_bdd`: windows `w_N` and Fatou).
  Ingredients: disjointness of the good-set bumps (`liftChiT_center_unique`,
  `cosetSymbol_eq_of_liftChiT`), Bessel (`eLpNorm_sqrt_sum_liftD_two_le`), Young for the cutoff
  (`eLpNorm_fourierInv_mul_liftChiT_le`, uniform `‖𝓕⁻ χ̃_s‖₁`), lower Khintchine
  (`eLpNorm_sqrt_sum_le_of_rademacher`) and `lift_transference`.
* Blueprint Lemma 9.4 (`lem:liftenvelope`): `lift_envelope` (pointwise, uniform in `j, μ, α`) and
  `lift_envelope_sup` (the supremum at fixed `s`), from the general kernel bound
  `norm_latMult_liftSym_fourier_le` (`|H| ≤ K B_R` gives
